@okuyam2y Thanks that works but I also had to add the output limit otherwise it crashed, now it works

```
"anthropic": {
            "models": {
                "claude-opus-4-6": {
                    "limit": {
                        "context": 200000,
                        "output": 100000
                    }
                }
            }
        },
```

@rekram1-node looks like the right thing. 

> the extra user message we send after a compaction is completed to basically help make the session auto continue (cause sometimes the llm wont do too much w/ just the summary)

I was asking me: by overriding compact agent could we improve instructions so the summary becomes better for continuation, or are there such big technical reasons that would make this not so useful?

Session ID is present in the following (at least with Opencode 1.4.3):

```ts
import type { Plugin } from "@opencode-ai/plugin";

const serviceName = "log-session";

export const LogSession: Plugin = async ({ project, client }) => {
  return {
    "experimental.chat.system.transform": async (input, output) => {
      console.log("system messages", input.sessionID, output.system);
    },
  };
};
```
